      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made strongly correlated materials quantitatively tractable and transformed comparison between many-body theory and measured spectra.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Vollhardt, and Kotliar are central architects of the modern method, though its development rests on a wider theoretical lineage.",
        "maturity": "It is an established, reproducible framework used broadly for correlated-electron materials, with clearly characterized domains of validity.",
        "uncertainties": [
