        "Bart J. van Wees",
        "Henk van Houten",
        "Michael Pepper"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Conductance quantization gave a remarkably direct experimental manifestation of quantum transport and established mesoscopic electronics as a field.",
        "attribution": "The named scientists made seminal quantum-point-contact observations, although independent near-contemporaneous work makes priority and allocation delicate.",
        "maturity": "The effect is textbook physics, reproduced across platforms and foundational for nanostructure transport.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Independent discovery and the appropriate balance among experimental groups require scrutiny."
